[TITLE]
;;Project Title/Notes
Drexel University campus (University City, Philadelphia): demo model
With LID: green roofs, permeable pavement and bioretention.
Subcatchments: Drexel-owned PWD parcels; impervious cover from city building footprints plus assumed paving.
Pipes are ASSUMED (street centrelines, 5-yr rational sizing); the real sewers here are combined.
Storm: NOAA Atlas 14 2-yr 24-hr (3.26 in), NRCS Type II. Ground: USGS 3DEP 1 m lidar.

[OPTIONS]
;;Option             Value
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
INFILTRATION         HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING         DYNWAVE
LINK_OFFSETS         DEPTH
MIN_SLOPE            0
ALLOW_PONDING        NO
SKIP_STEADY_STATE    NO
START_DATE           06/01/2024
START_TIME           00:00:00
REPORT_START_DATE    06/01/2024
REPORT_START_TIME    00:00:00
END_DATE             06/02/2024
END_TIME             06:00:00
SWEEP_START          01/01
SWEEP_END            12/31
DRY_DAYS             5
REPORT_STEP          00:05:00
WET_STEP             00:01:00
DRY_STEP             00:05:00
ROUTING_STEP         0:00:05
INERTIAL_DAMPING     PARTIAL
NORMAL_FLOW_LIMITED  BOTH
FORCE_MAIN_EQUATION  H-W
VARIABLE_STEP        0.75
LENGTHENING_STEP     0
MIN_SURFAREA         12.566
MAX_TRIALS           8
HEAD_TOLERANCE       0.005
SYS_FLOW_TOL         5
LAT_FLOW_TOL         5
MINIMUM_STEP         0.5
THREADS              1

[EVAPORATION]
;;Data Source    Parameters
CONSTANT         0.0
DRY_ONLY         NO

[RAINGAGES]
;;Name           Format    Interval SCF      Source
RG1              INTENSITY 0:05     1.0      TIMESERIES 2yr24hr

